{
    "chapter_num": 41,
    "verses_count": 26,
    "paragraphs_list": [
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 1,
                    "num_str": "1",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Then he brought me to the nave, and measured the jambs; on each side six cubits was the breadth of the jambs."
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Compare Gk: Heb tent"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 2,
                    "num_str": "2",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And the breadth of the entrance was ten cubits; and the sidewalls of the entrance were five cubits on either side; and he measured the length of the nave forty cubits, and its breadth, twenty cubits. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 3,
                    "num_str": "3",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Then he went into the inner room and measured the jambs of the entrance, two cubits; and the breadth of the entrance, six cubits; and the sidewalls"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Gk: Heb breadth"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " of the entrance, seven cubits. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 4,
                    "num_str": "4",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And he measured the length of the room, twenty cubits, and its breadth, twenty cubits, beyond the nave. And he said to me, “This is the most holy place.”"
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 5,
                    "num_str": "5",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Then he measured the wall of the temple, six cubits thick; and the breadth of the side chambers, four cubits, round about the temple. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 6,
                    "num_str": "6",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And the side chambers were in three stories, one over another, thirty in each story. There were offsets"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Gk Compare 1 Kings 6.6: Heb they entered"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " all around the wall of the temple to serve as supports for the side chambers, so that they should not be supported by the wall of the temple. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 7,
                    "num_str": "7",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And the side chambers became broader as they rose"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Cn: Heb it was surrounded"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " from story to story, corresponding to the enlargement of the offset"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Gk: Heb for the encompassing of the temple"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " from story to story round about the temple; on the side of the temple a stairway led upward, and thus one went up from the lowest story to the top story through the middle story. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 8,
                    "num_str": "8",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "I saw also that the temple had a raised platform round about; the foundations of the side chambers measured a full reed of six long cubits. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 9,
                    "num_str": "9",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "The thickness of the outer wall of the side chambers was five cubits; and the part of the platform which was left free was five cubits."
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Syr: Heb lacks five cubits"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " Between the platform"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Cn: Heb house of the side chambers"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " of the temple and the "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 10,
                    "num_str": "10",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "chambers of the court was a breadth of twenty cubits round about the temple on every side. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 11,
                    "num_str": "11",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And the doors of the side chambers opened on the part of the platform that was left free, one door toward the north, and another door toward the south; and the breadth of the part that was left free was five cubits round about."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 12,
                    "num_str": "12",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "The building that was facing the temple yard on the west side was seventy cubits broad; and the wall of the building was five cubits thick round about, and its length ninety cubits."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 13,
                    "num_str": "13",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Then he measured the temple, a hundred cubits long; and the yard and the building with its walls, a hundred cubits long; "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 14,
                    "num_str": "14",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "also the breadth of the east front of the temple and the yard, a hundred cubits."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 15,
                    "num_str": "15",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Then he measured the length of the building facing the yard which was at the west and its walls"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Cn: The meaning of the Hebrew term is unknown"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " on either side, a hundred cubits."
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "LINE_BREAK",
                            "text": "\n"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "The nave of the temple and the inner room and the outer"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Gk: Heb of the court"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " vestibule "
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 16,
                    "num_str": "16",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "were paneled"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Gk: Heb the thresholds"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " and round about all three had windows with recessed"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Cn Compare Gk 1 Kings 6.4: The meaning of the Hebrew term is unknown"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " frames. Over against the threshold the temple was paneled with wood round about, from the floor up to the windows (now the windows were covered), "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 17,
                    "num_str": "17",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "to the space above the door, even to the inner room, and on the outside. And on all the walls round about in the inner room and the nave were carved likenesses"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Cn: Heb measures and carved"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 18,
                    "num_str": "18",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "of cherubim and palm trees, a palm tree between cherub and cherub. Every cherub had two faces: "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 19,
                    "num_str": "19",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "the face of a man toward the palm tree on the one side, and the face of a young lion toward the palm tree on the other side. They were carved on the whole temple round about; "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 20,
                    "num_str": "20",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "from the floor to above the door cherubim and palm trees were carved on the wall."
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Cn Compare verse 25: Heb and the wall"
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 21,
                    "num_str": "21",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "The doorposts of the nave were squared; and in front of the holy place was something resembling "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 22,
                    "num_str": "22",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "an altar of wood, three cubits high, two cubits long, and two cubits broad;"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Gk: Heb lacks two cubits broad"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " its corners, its base,"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Gk: Heb length"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " and its walls were of wood. He said to me, “This is the table which is before the "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "SMALL_CAPS",
                            "text": "Lord"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": ".” "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 23,
                    "num_str": "23",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "The nave and the holy place had each a double door. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 24,
                    "num_str": "24",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "The doors had two leaves apiece, two swinging leaves for each door. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 25,
                    "num_str": "25",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And on the doors of the nave were carved cherubim and palm trees, such as were carved on the walls; and there was a canopy of wood in front of the vestibule outside. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 26,
                    "num_str": "26",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And there were recessed windows and palm trees on either side, on the sidewalls of the vestibule."
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Cn: Heb vestibule. And the side chambers of the temple and the canopies"
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        }
    ]
}